# 10. Domain-First Rule

AEGIS must not be implemented as thirteen disconnected pages.

The architecture must flow conceptually as:

```text
DOMAIN
   ↓
STATE
   ↓
EVENTS
   ↓
DATA CONTRACTS
   ↓
API CONTRACTS
   ↓
APPLICATION SERVICES
   ↓
FEATURES
   ↓
SCREENS
   ↓
COMPONENTS
```

A screen is a projection of the system.

A screen is **not** the source of business truth.

---

# 11. Business Logic Boundary

## Forbidden

Business-critical decisions must not be hidden inside individual screen components.

Avoid patterns such as:

```text
Screen
 └── determines threat severity
```

Prefer:

```text
Domain / application logic
        ↓
State / event
        ↓
Screen renders resulting state
```

The UI may initiate actions and present decisions, but it must not silently create conflicting domain truth.

