# 19. AEGIS Design-System Boundary

The AEGIS design system is the final visual authority.

External libraries are implementation tools.

Therefore:

```text
AEGIS Design Language
        ↓
Component rules
        ↓
Library implementation
```

Not:

```text
Ant Design defaults
+
shadcn defaults
+
random custom CSS
=
AEGIS
```

The second approach will produce visual inconsistency and long-term maintenance debt.

---

# 20. Spatial UI Boundary

The 3D layer should be treated as a specialized visualization subsystem.

It should not absorb ordinary application concerns.

Conceptually:

```text
AEGIS Application
│
├── Operational UI
│
├── Data / State
│
└── Spatial Visualization
      ├── Scene
      ├── Camera
      ├── Terrain
      ├── Layers
      ├── Markers
      └── Interaction
```

The spatial layer consumes approved domain/state information.

It must not independently invent threat state.

